draw pairs. B5 is a duplicate, which could be useful for a pair or Pung. T2 is less useful.  \n\nAfter evaluating, the best discard is T2 because:  \n1. It's a simple tile with no immediate sequence potential in hand (T2 needs T1 or T3/T4, and T3 is exhausted with 0 left unseen).  \n2. It doesn't contribute to high-value patterns like All Types (which needs all suits and honors) as much as keeping honors might.  \n3. It reduces clutter in the Bamboo suit, allowing focus on Dots or honors.  \n\nAnswer: Play T2"}
